{#
  THINGS TO DO: the engraved hero (approved Round 5 artwork), then seven chapters.

  Each chapter is its own section and takes its height from its content. Inside it:
    .fg-ground    its own illustrated layer: a crop of Painting A (chapters 1-3) or parchment (4-7, until
                  Paintings B and C), over a ground colour taken from the crop's edge
    .fg-trailseg  its piece of the gold trail, down the margin through the chapter's number
    .fg-c         its content, on a grid (desktop) or stacked (tablet and phone)
  Each chapter starts --in above the end of the one before, sits on top of it and fades its ground in over
  that overlap. Content never enters an overlap (--out at the bottom of each chapter matches the next --in).
  On desktop the ground of chapters 2 and 3 (and the map pins on it) drift together, about 4% slower than the
  page, and the photo prints lift about 1% faster: CSS scroll-driven animation, off for reduced motion,
  off below 1100 px, and simply absent in browsers without it.
  Painting A: art-masters/things-to-do/painting-a (unchanged); its crops come from scripts/ttd-art.mjs.
  ?slots outlines the empty artwork slots that remain; ?ref overlays the original reference.
#}
{%- set ps = "(min-width:1100px) 17vw, 62vw" -%}
<main id="main" class="fg">

{# ================================================================= HERO #}
<header class="fg-sec fg-hero" id="top" style="--h:309">
  <picture class="fg-hero-art">
    <source media="(max-width:699px)" type="image/avif" width="3045" height="2688" sizes="100vw"
      srcset="/assets/ttd/hero/phone-480.avif 480w, /assets/ttd/hero/phone-780.avif 780w, /assets/ttd/hero/phone-1170.avif 1170w">
    <source media="(max-width:699px)" type="image/webp" width="3045" height="2688" sizes="100vw"
      srcset="/assets/ttd/hero/phone-480.webp 480w, /assets/ttd/hero/phone-780.webp 780w, /assets/ttd/hero/phone-1170.webp 1170w">
    <source type="image/avif" sizes="100vw"
      srcset="/assets/ttd/hero/scene-960.avif 960w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-1440.avif 1440w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-1920.avif 1920w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-2560.avif 2560w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-3200.avif 3200w">
    <source type="image/webp" sizes="100vw"
      srcset="/assets/ttd/hero/scene-960.webp 960w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-1440.webp 1440w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-1920.webp 1920w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-2560.webp 2560w, /assets/ttd/hero/scene-3200.webp 3200w">
    <img src="/assets/ttd/hero/scene-1920.jpg" width="6344" height="2688" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
      alt="Engraved illustration of Eagle&rsquo;s Nest Resort at sunrise: the lodge&rsquo;s glass gable among spruce and aspen above a rocky shore, a wooden dock with a person fishing from a small boat, and geese flying over Anahim Lake.">
  </picture>
  <h1 class="fg-a fg-h1" style="--x:47;--y:26;--w:320">
    <span class="fg-eyebrow">Anahim Lake <span aria-hidden="true">•</span> West Chilcotin</span>
    <span class="fg-h1-main">There&rsquo;s a<br> lot out here.</span>
  </h1>
  <p class="fg-a fg-lede" style="--x:47;--y:133;--w:270">
    <span>Paddle out from the dock. Watch the pelicans come in.</span>
    <span>Cast a line, find a trail or head farther into the Chilcotin.</span>
    <span>And when the lake freezes, come back and do it all differently.</span>
  </p>
</header>

